Umm... It seems it's not working for `playground/vue-legacy/module.vue` (async chunk).
`module` is the second argument of `System.register` callback but rollup outputs `function (exports) {` instead of `function (exports, module) {`, when `module` isn't used.
```js
// assets/module-legacy.hash.js
;

(function () {
  System.register(['./index-legacy.a53ab904.js'], function (exports) {
    'use strict';

    var __vite_style__ = document.createElement('style');

    __vite_style__.innerHTML = "\n.container[data-v-82673ce5] {\n  height: 100vh;\n  background: url('" + new URL('asset.b9f46fb3.png', module.meta.url).href + "') no-repeat;\n  background-size: contain;\n  background-position: center;\n}\n";
    document.head.appendChild(__vite_style__);
```

`arguments` will have a different value if it's inside a different function. So I guess it's not safe to use.

```js
System.register('', function () {
  function bar () {
    console.log(arguments[1].meta.url) // here
  }
  bar()
})
```
